      "content": "The simulation results are in. The 4.2-second latency is a massive problem. According to the models, a pressure spike during that window would cause a breach in the secondary containment protocols before a human can even react. The risk of a thermal excursion is significantly higher under manual control.\n\nSince we have to go through with the regulator's update tomorrow, how do we mitigate this risk? Is there any way to keep the system in automated mode during high-load periods to prevent this?",
